course: dictionary
lesson: 5803
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Magazine is one of them. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The magazine by the shop till» is a thin paper book with stories and pictures, because you buy it at a till and it is printed. You would not pay for a gun part at a till.
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «My favourite magazine comes out every month» fits a paper book. «The magazine was empty, so the gun could not fire» fits the gun part. Ask yourself: what is the topic of the sentence? The topic will point to the right meaning.
explain: Magazines are also a kind of reading. They are non-fiction, which means they are full of real facts, articles and reports. «Gaming guides, magazines and fact books are real reading too.» Reading what you enjoy is still reading, and it helps you learn new words.
explain: Some magazines carry adverts, and adverts do not always tell the truth. «Magazines that circle bits of a star's body in red» show a picture that has been changed. When you read a magazine, ask: is this true, or is it trying to sell me something?
fact: A magazine is a thin book with a paper cover, full of articles, stories and pictures.
fact: A magazine comes out every week or every month, so you can have a weekly or monthly magazine.
fact: Magazine can also mean a TV or radio programme with many short reports.
fact: «Printed pictures in books and magazines are made of tiny dots of four inks, cyan, magenta, yellow and black.»
fact: Some magazines have adverts, and not everything in them is true.
exercise: «The magazine by the shop till was full of celebrity stories.» What is a magazine in this sentence? | The part of a gun that holds the bullets | A store for weapons and explosives | *A thin paper book of stories and pictures that comes out regularly | A radio programme with short reports
exercise: «The magazine was empty, so the gun could not fire.» What does magazine mean here? | A shop that sells guns | A weekly paper book with pictures | *The part of a gun that holds the bullets | A TV show with many short reports
exercise: «Printed pictures in books and magazines are made of tiny dots of four inks.» How many inks are there? | Two | Three | *Four | Ten
test: Which phrase means a magazine that comes out once a month? | *a monthly magazine | a magazine article | a weekly magazine | a magazine picture
test: Ruby says magazines are not real reading. Which answer is best? | Magazines are always completely true | Magazines are not reading at all | *Magazines are real reading, and interest is what keeps a reader going | Magazines are only for babies
exam: Which sentence shows that not everything in a magazine is true? | Magazines have stories and pictures in them | Magazines are printed on paper | A magazine comes out every week | *Some magazine adverts make things look better than they really are
